out/
*.db
*.destroyed.json
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Never commit a key or a crosswalk. The .gitignore is a backstop, not the
# control -- the real control is that these live outside the repo entirely.
*.blob
dev-vault.key

# Contracts the installer and demos generate. Regenerated on every run, so a
# committed copy is only ever stale -- and demo.approved.yaml carries a real
# approval signature over synthetic rules, which is precisely the thing that
# must not be sitting in a repo looking like someone's sign-off.
contracts/demo.yaml
contracts/demo.approved.yaml

# The virtualenv setup creates.
.venv/

# Working files from reviewing real drops. Contracts, plans and drafts made
# from a real extract name the study and describe its columns; this repository
# holds the tool, not any study's paperwork. Keep them beside the data, under
# the same access controls. Root-anchored so the tool's own files are unaffected.
/*.draft.yaml
/test*.yaml
/*_plan.csv
/*.patch
/deidkit-*.md
/Claude outputs/
